.TH CPU 1
.SH NAME
cpu \- run a command on a Linux host, in this name space
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpu
[
.B -h
.I host
] [
.B -c
.I cmd args ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Cpu
runs a command on
.IR host ,
or the host named in
.B $cpu
if there is no
.B -h
option, a Linux machine that sees the name space
.I cpu
runs in, as Plan 9's cpu server does.
The command's standard input, output and error are
.IR cpu 's,
and its exit status is
.IR cpu 's.
Its directory is
.IR cpu 's
working directory: the host's own, if it has one by that name,
else this name space's, under
.BR /mnt/term .
.PP
With
.BR -c ,
the rest of the command line is run by the host's
.IR sh .
Without, the user's login shell runs on a pseudo-terminal,
.I cpu
makes its own terminal raw, and the size is
.IR ptty 's
(see
.IR vt (1)),
else
.B $COLS
and
.BR $LINES .
.PP
A host is named in
.BR $home/lib/cpu ,
then
.BR /lib/cpu ,
files in the format of
.IR ndb (6):
.IP
.EX
cpu=build1 cmd="ssh build1"
cpu=app cmd="ssh build1 docker exec -i app" ns=/lib/namespace.untrusted
.EE
.PP
.B cmd
is the host's transport, an
.IR rc (1)
command line that, given a command, runs it on the host
with the transport's standard input and output:
.IR ssh (1),
or a container runtime's
.BR "exec -i" .
.PP
.I Cpu
needs the
.B u9cpu
package (see
.IR pkg (1)),
as
.B ssh
needs its own.
Each
.I cpu
has a session of its own, which runs the transport twice, by
.IR ferry (1),
which ships
.I u9cpu
to the host: once with
.BR "u9cpu -n" ,
to which
.IR exportfs (4)
serves
.IR cpu 's
name space, and once with
.BR "u9cpu -c -n" ,
which serves the host's commands as Inferno's
.IR cmd (3)
does.
.I Cpu
mounts the second on
.BR /mnt/cpu ,
in a name space of its own, and makes its command by its
.BR clone .
The session lasts until either stream ends or
.I cpu
does.
If the host has
.BR ns= ,
the name space exported is one made from that file by
.I newns
(see
.IR auth (2)
and
.IR namespace (6)).
.PP
On the host,
.I u9cpu
makes the name space, in a user and mount name space of the host's,
by FUSE: the host's root, with this name space at
.B /mnt/term
and its
.BI /usr/ user
at
.BI /usr/ user\f1.
A host with no FUSE refuses it, and
.I cpu
fails with the reason.
.SH FILES
.TF $home/lib/cpu
.TP
.B /lib/cpu
hosts
.TP
.B $home/lib/cpu
the user's hosts, searched first
.PD
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B src/cmd/cpu.c
and
.B src/u9cpu
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ferry (1),
.IR pkg (1),
.IR ssh (1),
.IR vt (1),
.IR exportfs (4),
.IR ndb (6)
.SH BUGS
The session sees the name space as it was when
.I cpu
started; binds and mounts made later are not reflected.
.PP
A change in the window's size is not passed on.
.PP
An interrupt ends
.BR "cpu -c" ,
and its command is killed, not sent
.BR SIGINT .
